I just put up the remaining stock from the last production run on the Refle=
ctacles website. These were pulled before I sold out completely so I didn't=
 oversell and get people yelling at me (as people tend to do these days). T=
here is not much, but you might find what you are looking for. Some IRpair =
frames, some IRcloak, and the Universal IRclip from the 2016 production run=
 that are now 2 for the price of one (they have a more noticeable logo on t=
he lens and some might even call them collector's items these days). I also=
 just received a rush order of light and dark lenses for the Ghost and Phan=
tom, so I will sell those until the supply of lenses is gone. But check out=
 the site and see what is there at the moment.

If you don't see what you want right now, don't stress. Everything should b=
e fully restocked at the end of August. There will be new additions to the =
IRpair Turtles collection with some really neat colors. Updates will be ann=
ounced through this newsletter so please stay tuned if you are interested.

Please stick in there with me on shipping out the orders. Packages will be =
shipped once a week in the order received. I'll do my best to get them all =
out in a timely manner, but please understand it is only me around here doi=
ng it all (I prefer it that way). If you all swamp me out with orders quick=
ly, just know that I have been doing this particular business for over ten =
years now and have always delivered on my word. Just please be patient and =
I will ship out as soon as I can.

Lastly, please try to find answers to your questions on the website. I do m=
y best to respond to all emails but it can take some time since I personall=
y respond to every one and I don't use some stupid fucking AI email bot gar=
bage. When I get asked, "When will these be in stock again", I simply respo=
nd over and over, please sign up to the newsletter to be informed all all n=
ews (I think it says this on the website in at least four different places)=
=2E So if you don't find what you want=20=
this time, just hang in there and pay=20=
attention to the newsletter because more is coming soon. With this said, I'=
ll always respond to your emails, but it may take some time. Patience is so=
mething that we have lost with the internet in our pocket.

Let me leave you with a few thoughts on taking it slow. These are not meant=
 to be inspiring or profound, but rather just a bit of advice from the P.I.=
E. (Pre Internet Era (ish)).

"Said, woman, take it slow, it'll work itself out fine
All we need is just a little patience
Said, sugar, make it slow and we'll come together fine
All we need is just a little patience
Patience. Mm, yeah"
-Axel Rose, 1989.

"Good things come to those who wait"
-Guinness, 1996.

"The best things come to those who wait"
-H. J. Heinz Company, 1987.

"I have mastered the art of procrastination"
-I think I said that, 2026.

Take it easy and enjoy while you can.
S.



















